narrative:
## Delegating Work to Helper Functions

A good program is like a well-organized team: each function has one clear job. The `main` function acts as the manager, calling helpers to get things done.

### A Program with Helpers

```xiom
fn print_header() {
  io.println("===================");
  io.println("  EVENT PLANNER");
  io.println("===================");
}

fn print_invite(name: Str) {
  io.println("Inviting: ");
  io.println(name);
}

fn calc_cost(guests: Int, per_person: Int) -> Int {
  return guests * per_person;
}

fn main() {
  print_header();

  io.println("Guest list:");
  print_invite("Alice");
  print_invite("Bob");
  print_invite("Charlie");

  let total: Int = calc_cost(3, 15);
  io.println("Total cost: ");
  io.println(total);
}
```

Each function has ONE job:
- `print_header()` — shows the title banner
- `print_invite(name)` — invites one person
- `calc_cost(guests, per_person)` — calculates the total cost

`main` orchestrates everything by calling helpers in order. To change how invitations look, you only edit one function. To change cost calculations, you edit another. Clean, organized, and easy to maintain!

